+### 12.5 The residual of the review 507f49b7 (`ENV-SECTOR-HEIGHT-WITNESS-CONSUMER-JOIN-1`): the consumed reference's physical words and effective setup
+
+The SAME review closed the three other corrections at source and left two facts of the consumer join open; this section states their correction. Test-only: `lua/sector-height-witness.lua`, its scripted tests, this contract. No C, Rust product, build, Cargo or compiled input changed.
+
+- **Every field a claim consumes is validated before anything happens.** A `clearance_original` reference (`original=`) and a paired `clearance_control` reference (`control=`) are read whole and then checked field by field before the output file, the boot or the intervention: the counts record (`windows`, `windows_without_handoff`, `scan_reads`,
+  `height_reads`, `altered_windows`, `altered_reads`, `handoffs`, `unbound_lookaheads`, `frames`: canonical whole numbers); the hand-off record (`ordinal`, `window`, `reads`, `phase` 0..3, `host_id`, `sector`, `real_word`/`answered_word` as `none` or one raw word, and the four physical words `elevation`, `min_height`, `pre_y`, `answered_y` as FINITE raw words:
+  eight hex digits, exponent field not all ones); for a control also the trajectory record and the pairing record with its field list, no altered window or read, and a host that answered. An absent, `nil`, short, non-hex, infinite, NaN, duplicate or out-of-domain field is a refusal naming the field. The original profile's first hand-off legitimately has window 0, no reads and no sector and the host never asked.
+  A physical or hand-off effect (`sh-witness-effect`) is claimed only between two real finite words; a missing word never means "changed".
+- **The effective setup is bound.** Schema 3 reports carry the EFFECTIVE `campaign` (the override or the scenario's script) and `map` the run really boots, next to scenario, seed, frame and hours; `campaign=` and `map=` overrides must be single tokens. Original, control and intervention must have the same semantic setup (the fresh root's path is not part of it: two roots are
+  separate paths of one setup); matching defaults and explicitly matching overrides are the same setup, a different campaign or map is refused before any effect. A save report is the exception for the campaign only: it names the ORIGINAL campaign, while the load boots the generated saved script `<name>.S..`, so the load binds the saved name relation, the map and the seeds and requires the save report to name a campaign.
+  The finiteness rule is ONLY for these physical fields: the saved raw HEIGHT histories of M6 (a quiet NaN, an infinity, a negative word) are untouched.
+- **Controls** (`tests/sector_height_witness_driver.rs`): positive first (the coherent pair, the valid changed-word run with a stated real effect, the explicit-default override pair, the save-to-generated-script load with NaN and infinite seeds), then ONE removal or ONE damage at a time: each physical word dropped, `nil`, short, non-hex, infinite, NaN; host id, phase, ordinal, sector, counts, trajectory; a changed effective campaign or map of the control, the original, the run or the save report. Each is refused with no output and no log.
